WEBVTT

00:39.620 --> 00:41.121
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

00:41.956 --> 00:43.165
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

01:37.469 --> 01:38.762
Water--

01:38.846 --> 01:41.098
Oh, this place.

01:42.099 --> 01:44.768
If you go a little past
that elevated track,

01:44.852 --> 01:46.687
there's an underground entrance.

01:46.770 --> 01:48.605
Water gets collected over there.

01:49.189 --> 01:50.649
[Kiruko] Thanks for the help.

01:51.317 --> 01:54.111
Hey, do you need a place to sleep?

01:54.194 --> 01:55.195
HOTEL
CLEAN FUTONS

01:55.279 --> 01:58.574
I have clean rooms
and aired-out futons, you know.

01:59.575 --> 02:01.910
Sorry, but we're just passing through.

02:04.455 --> 02:05.789
I see.

02:07.583 --> 02:08.667
Well,

02:08.751 --> 02:13.672
it'd be good to leave our bags
while we get water.

02:13.756 --> 02:15.716
Since the water will be heavy.

02:19.386 --> 02:21.722
[Maru] You did that
just to give her money.

02:22.306 --> 02:25.017
You're too nice.
What if she steals everything?

02:25.100 --> 02:27.811
We don't have anything worth stealing.

02:28.812 --> 02:32.358
She even told us to take our money
and valuables with us.

02:32.441 --> 02:33.776
<i>Let's trust her.</i>

02:33.859 --> 02:34.860
100% SAFE WATER

02:36.111 --> 02:37.237
[Maru] Look.

02:37.988 --> 02:40.282
Isn't this it? The underground entrance.

02:47.373 --> 02:49.958
BICYCLE PARKING - OPEN 24 HOURS

02:53.670 --> 02:55.547
[water dripping]

02:59.426 --> 03:00.636
It's water.

03:00.719 --> 03:04.098
But isn't it just collecting here?

03:04.181 --> 03:06.016
It doesn't look very clean.

03:09.520 --> 03:11.397
SUBWAY

03:11.480 --> 03:13.023
Someone's collapsed over there!

03:13.607 --> 03:15.818
Maru! Don't jump
recklessly into the water!

03:31.166 --> 03:33.127
That looks really bad.

03:33.210 --> 03:34.670
Is he still alive?

03:34.753 --> 03:35.754
[stranger] My buddy…

03:36.255 --> 03:38.048
Help my buddy.

03:39.133 --> 03:42.678
It was a monster.

03:43.804 --> 03:45.180
My buddy…

03:45.264 --> 03:46.765
Help…

04:06.994 --> 04:09.705
-That guy's a goner.
-Sis.

04:13.250 --> 04:15.210
[howling]

04:18.547 --> 04:19.548
Run!

04:23.010 --> 04:25.012
[both panting]

04:40.944 --> 04:42.779
[panting heavily]

04:47.201 --> 04:48.619
[clicks tongue]

04:53.665 --> 04:55.334
[huffing]

05:03.800 --> 05:05.677
-It worked.
-Huh?

05:07.179 --> 05:09.640
[Kiruko] It took an extra shot, but…

05:10.682 --> 05:12.351
Look. It's out cold.

05:12.434 --> 05:13.769
Oh!

05:13.852 --> 05:17.022
Once you know it's gonna chase you,
it's easy to come up with a plan.

05:17.105 --> 05:20.067
[Maru]
Your quick thinking is really amazing.

05:20.150 --> 05:21.485
[Kiruko chuckles]

05:22.611 --> 05:24.571
Hurry up and kill it, Maru.

05:24.655 --> 05:25.864
Oh, right.

05:27.199 --> 05:28.200
All right.

05:29.618 --> 05:31.578
Fatal Dive!

05:31.662 --> 05:36.708
[echoing] <i>Fatal Dive! Fatal Dive!
Fatal Dive! Fatal Dive!</i>

05:41.171 --> 05:42.214
Huh?

05:42.297 --> 05:43.382
Huh?

05:43.882 --> 05:45.300
[soft howl]

05:46.176 --> 05:47.177
Why…

05:48.011 --> 05:50.764
It's not a Hiruko! It's a wild animal!

05:50.847 --> 05:53.976
[Kiruko] W-What? No way!

05:54.059 --> 05:55.060
Over there, Maru!

05:55.143 --> 05:56.979
[Maru] Sis, wait!

05:57.062 --> 05:58.313
[Kiruko] Here. Hurry up!

05:58.397 --> 05:59.565
[Maru] W-wait!

05:59.648 --> 06:01.692
-[Kiruko] Climb up!
-[Maru whimpers]

06:11.493 --> 06:13.704
[Kiruko] Good thing
I managed to get up here.

06:15.330 --> 06:16.623
[both gasp]

06:17.457 --> 06:19.710
-It's a bear! A bear!
-It's a bear! A bear!

06:19.793 --> 06:21.712
Can you imagine how that felt, Sis?

06:21.795 --> 06:24.131
Just when I was thinking,

06:24.214 --> 06:26.717
"Huh? It's not going in. That's weird."

06:26.800 --> 06:29.720
I met the bear's eyes from this distance!

06:29.803 --> 06:31.555
Sorry! Sorry! Sorry!

06:31.638 --> 06:33.932
That guy said it was a monster!

06:34.016 --> 06:36.226
[Maru] Don't blame it on someone else!

06:36.310 --> 06:38.729
That bear basically is a monster!

06:41.523 --> 06:45.027
But it's a good thing it's a bear.
It can't climb up.

06:45.110 --> 06:46.653
We'd be done for if it was a gorilla.

06:48.113 --> 06:49.698
[Maru groans]

06:55.078 --> 06:56.079
[Kiruko] Not good.

06:56.580 --> 06:58.290
It's getting cold.

06:59.833 --> 07:01.710
Wait. Where did the bear go?

07:01.793 --> 07:05.589
It kept walking around, but it's gone now.

07:05.672 --> 07:07.382
Let's take the chance to get away.

07:11.553 --> 07:14.431
If the fourth bullet fires,
I've got one shot left.

07:14.514 --> 07:17.517
-Will it shoot?
-Mmm.

07:18.143 --> 07:19.436
I'll warm up the battery.

07:23.815 --> 07:24.816
Uh-oh.

07:24.900 --> 07:26.610
What? "Uh-oh"?

07:28.737 --> 07:29.946
Three choices.

07:30.447 --> 07:33.033
One. I dropped the battery.

07:33.742 --> 07:35.535
Two. Well--

07:36.495 --> 07:38.330
That is--

07:38.413 --> 07:40.165
What are you doing?

07:41.625 --> 07:44.044
Geez, it really fell.

07:44.670 --> 07:46.421
-[Kiruko] Go get it.
-Stop joking.

07:46.505 --> 07:48.757
What if the bear is still around?

07:50.425 --> 07:51.677
[Kiruko] Maru.

07:52.260 --> 07:56.181
Do you see me as a woman? Or a man?

07:56.264 --> 07:58.934
What? What's with that question?

08:01.269 --> 08:04.481
Well, you look like a woman, so--

08:05.065 --> 08:08.110
I guess that's probably
not what you want to hear, but…

08:08.193 --> 08:09.194
Okay!

08:10.028 --> 08:12.614
I'll let you touch my boobs
if you get it--

08:14.700 --> 08:15.826
He jumped!

08:15.909 --> 08:17.828
That idiot!

08:20.414 --> 08:21.456
Heh.

08:23.041 --> 08:24.376
-Maru!
-[howling]

08:24.459 --> 08:26.002
There it is!

08:26.086 --> 08:28.004
[grunting]

08:29.881 --> 08:31.007
[groans]

08:34.594 --> 08:36.847
It was hiding and waiting
for us to come down.

08:37.431 --> 08:38.890
It's definitely targeting us.

08:39.725 --> 08:41.476
We can wait it out forever up here

08:42.060 --> 08:44.396
or get down and shoot it
when it's in range.

08:44.479 --> 08:45.772
[Kiruko] Damn it.

08:46.857 --> 08:48.191
Maru,

08:48.692 --> 08:52.487
I managed to climb up
from the adrenaline rush,

08:52.988 --> 08:55.031
but I can't climb down from here.

08:55.741 --> 08:57.868
-What?
-No, see.

08:57.951 --> 09:00.370
It's not normal to be as tough as you.

09:00.454 --> 09:02.414
Normal people can't handle this height!

09:02.914 --> 09:04.416
So Maru,

09:04.499 --> 09:08.587
this time, go down with the Kiru-Beam
and kill the bear.

09:09.296 --> 09:12.549
Then I'll use the dead bear as a cushion
and get down.

09:15.093 --> 09:18.638
As long as it's not a Man-eater,
all you need is one shot to the head.

09:19.639 --> 09:22.309
Let me tell you one thing, Sis.

09:22.392 --> 09:27.230
Even if you give me the gun,
I can't shoot as accurately as you.

09:28.064 --> 09:30.233
Am I that good of a shot?

09:30.317 --> 09:32.027
Yeah, you're really good.

09:32.110 --> 09:34.738
Normally, you can't shoot a power pole
while climbing a fence

09:34.821 --> 09:37.783
or aim for the enemy's arm while running.

09:38.283 --> 09:40.577
Am I helpful?

09:40.660 --> 09:41.870
Of course you are.

09:41.953 --> 09:44.080
I would've died five times already
without you.

09:48.168 --> 09:49.169
Sis?

09:51.922 --> 09:53.715
I'm help--

09:54.674 --> 09:55.884
[Haruki] <i>I want to be helpful to Robin.</i>

09:55.967 --> 09:59.638
[Robin] <i>I'm not playing around!
I told you not to come. It's dangerous!</i>

09:59.721 --> 10:00.889
[Haruki] <i>I'll drive it away.</i>

10:00.972 --> 10:02.140
<i>I know I can do it.</i>

10:04.309 --> 10:05.477
[Kiruko] Okay!

10:06.478 --> 10:07.854
Let's make a new plan.

10:10.774 --> 10:15.570
<i>First, wait for the bear to get far away
while warming up our bodies.</i>

10:15.654 --> 10:17.155
[Maru] <i>And once it's far away?</i>

10:17.239 --> 10:20.033
<i>Maru, you use that chance to get down.</i>

10:21.451 --> 10:22.786
[groans]

10:23.328 --> 10:26.623
<i>I'll come down as soon as I hear you land.</i>

10:30.252 --> 10:31.795
[winces]

10:32.963 --> 10:35.340
-[Maru tuts]
-[both grunt, shout]

10:35.423 --> 10:38.760
[Kiruko] <i>Then you run as fast as you can
after catching me.</i>

10:39.678 --> 10:42.806
[Maru] <i>What about you?
What if the fourth shot doesn't fire?</i>

10:42.889 --> 10:44.766
[growling]

10:46.351 --> 10:47.602
[Kiruko] <i>If that happens…</i>

10:50.146 --> 10:52.941
<i>I'll hold it off until you get away.</i>

11:00.031 --> 11:01.658
[squelching]

11:09.541 --> 11:11.710
[sighs deeply]

11:11.793 --> 11:15.213
[panting]

11:19.009 --> 11:22.137
[gasps] Why didn't you get away?

11:23.513 --> 11:27.309
You actually thought
I'd run away alone? That hurts.

11:27.893 --> 11:29.477
And it was a flaw in your plan.

11:31.229 --> 11:33.148
[chuckles]

11:33.231 --> 11:36.401
I was confident
the fourth shot would fire.

11:36.484 --> 11:37.569
What?

11:38.570 --> 11:41.573
The battery was charged
with your horny energy!

11:41.656 --> 11:43.825
What the hell? Stop that!

11:43.909 --> 11:47.454
-[Kiruko laughing]
-Hey!

11:49.706 --> 11:52.542
[bystander 1] Iwata! Hang in there! Iwata!

11:53.543 --> 11:56.504
-Boss.
-[bystander 2] Shimomoto didn't make it.

11:56.588 --> 11:57.589
[bystander 3] Totori.

11:58.340 --> 12:00.508
What about the people who saved Iwata?

12:01.176 --> 12:05.180
They said their names weren't worth it
and left like the wind.

12:05.263 --> 12:06.556
[bystander 1] For real?

12:06.640 --> 12:09.809
Who were they? The bear's head
was completely blown away.

12:10.435 --> 12:11.436
HOTEL

12:11.519 --> 12:14.481
-[bystander 3] I wanted to meet them.
-[bystander 2] Yeah.

12:14.564 --> 12:17.067
To think there'd be a bear around here--

12:17.150 --> 12:18.944
It's so nice animals aren't like Hiruko.

12:19.027 --> 12:21.905
Their carcasses don't disappear
and we can eat them.

12:22.822 --> 12:26.368
I'll tell you how we got tricked,
so you can keep it in mind.

12:26.451 --> 12:27.661
We got tricked?

12:28.161 --> 12:32.290
[Kiruko] The vigilantes in the tent city
were also bandits.

12:33.500 --> 12:36.670
We were completely lured
into their hunting grounds.

12:37.295 --> 12:39.381
Lured?

12:39.464 --> 12:42.842
-100% safe water.
-[Maru gasps]

12:42.926 --> 12:45.136
[Kiruko] <i>I'm sure their plan was to block</i>

12:45.220 --> 12:47.847
<i>the underground entrance
once we got close.</i>

12:48.890 --> 12:51.643
That map-seller must've been in on it too.

12:51.726 --> 12:55.355
Then we can't trust anything on the map.

12:55.438 --> 12:58.191
It might not all be fake.

12:58.775 --> 13:01.611
That's enough regretting. Let's sleep.

13:02.195 --> 13:04.406
We're stuck here anyway.

13:05.991 --> 13:06.992
What's wrong?

13:07.075 --> 13:11.246
She gave us two rooms, so let's sleep
comfortably on our own.

13:12.580 --> 13:14.708
[Maru] Did you forget something?

13:14.791 --> 13:16.167
Huh?

13:16.251 --> 13:20.672
Did you forget about your promise, Sis?

13:23.967 --> 13:26.052
I risked my life, you know.

13:28.263 --> 13:30.098
Let me touch your boobs.

13:31.016 --> 13:33.435
HOTEL

13:33.518 --> 13:37.188
[Kiruko] My sister's hair was originally
black and straight.

13:37.814 --> 13:41.067
It seems your hair can change

13:41.151 --> 13:43.194
after undergoing surgery
for a major injury.

13:44.029 --> 13:49.784
That's probably why I started growing
this red, dry hair.

13:50.410 --> 13:52.787
But I think it's a curse from my sister.

13:54.039 --> 13:57.417
Saying "Don't mess with my body!"

13:58.001 --> 13:59.002
[Maru] I see.

14:00.211 --> 14:01.796
Now take off your jacket.

14:03.631 --> 14:09.179
You sure?
Touching my boobs means this, you know.

14:09.262 --> 14:12.515
If you still say it doesn't matter,
then I'll keep my promise.

14:12.599 --> 14:15.477
Because it's a promise between men!

14:18.646 --> 14:21.441
Wai-- Rules! Let's set some rules.

14:21.524 --> 14:22.609
Like how many sec--

14:24.652 --> 14:26.529
[both] <i>That sounded just like a girl.</i>

14:26.613 --> 14:27.614
[door opens]

14:28.531 --> 14:29.616
Hey, you two.

14:32.535 --> 14:34.454
PLEASE KEEP THE ROOMS CLEAN

14:35.830 --> 14:38.041
PLEASE DON'T DIRTY THE FUTON

14:38.124 --> 14:41.544
This is not the place for doing that!

14:42.170 --> 14:44.297
-You, come this way.
-Wait.

14:48.802 --> 14:50.053
Sir,

14:51.888 --> 14:53.932
how about me?

14:56.434 --> 14:57.769
Eight hundred thousand.

14:57.852 --> 15:00.188
Or that solar-powered light!

15:00.271 --> 15:01.272
That will be enough.

15:01.856 --> 15:03.900
So you did go through our stuff.

15:03.983 --> 15:06.402
I didn't take anything,
so what's the problem?

15:06.486 --> 15:08.321
So how about it?

15:08.404 --> 15:10.532
Should I keep the bandana on?

15:11.950 --> 15:14.953
Call me Totori. I don't know my last name.

15:15.036 --> 15:16.788
Hey, I'm good.

15:16.871 --> 15:18.915
Do you know what "no, thank you" means?

15:18.998 --> 15:20.291
I prefer older girls--

15:20.375 --> 15:21.543
[gasps]

15:23.169 --> 15:26.339
[heart beats]

15:33.721 --> 15:35.181
-[Maru gasps]
-[Totori shrieks]

15:35.974 --> 15:37.183
You--

15:37.267 --> 15:39.727
Sis! Get over here!

15:39.811 --> 15:40.937
[Totori] What're you doing?

15:41.020 --> 15:42.814
[Maru] Don't move.

15:42.897 --> 15:44.190
Sis!

15:44.816 --> 15:46.359
What's wrong, Maru?

15:46.943 --> 15:49.112
-I got in!
-Ouch! It hurts!

15:51.906 --> 15:54.200
What went in where?

15:57.203 --> 15:58.705
[gasps]

16:01.624 --> 16:03.418
What did you do?

16:04.961 --> 16:05.962
No…

16:07.005 --> 16:10.049
[narrator] <i>After realizing
the difficulties of having to explain</i>

16:10.133 --> 16:12.927
<i>the various misunderstandings
of this situation,</i>

16:13.428 --> 16:17.432
<i>all Maru could see was
the dark depths of his despair.</i>

16:19.601 --> 16:21.936
[medical robot]
<i>There are no signs of an illness.</i>

16:23.229 --> 16:26.191
Really? What a relief.

16:26.941 --> 16:30.778
<i>You show signs of fatigue.
Please take a nap here.</i>

16:31.279 --> 16:33.198
[students chattering]

16:37.744 --> 16:39.370
[grunts]

16:42.665 --> 16:43.917
[gasp]

16:46.794 --> 16:48.004
Who's there?

16:50.089 --> 16:52.342
[gasps] What?

16:57.555 --> 16:59.015
[yelps]

16:59.641 --> 17:00.934
[breathes shakily]

17:02.352 --> 17:03.394
Asura?

17:06.439 --> 17:09.651
What are you good at, Tokio?

17:11.486 --> 17:12.946
[Tokio] What do you mean?

17:18.785 --> 17:19.827
It disappeared.

17:23.790 --> 17:27.460
[gasps] What? My leg is--

17:28.044 --> 17:30.380
Doctor! Doctor!

17:32.757 --> 17:33.800
[gasps]

17:37.553 --> 17:38.554
A dream?

17:43.601 --> 17:44.936
How are you feeling?

17:45.436 --> 17:47.146
[Tokio] I'm fine.

17:52.068 --> 17:53.069
DON'T COME IN

17:53.152 --> 17:55.446
We are really sorry!

17:55.530 --> 17:57.699
[Maru] My heaven is right here.

17:57.782 --> 18:00.743
I will take full responsibility.
Please forgive me.

18:00.827 --> 18:05.039
Well, I don't mind
if we continue chatting like this.

18:05.123 --> 18:07.250
But you look so pitiful,
so let's stop here.

18:07.834 --> 18:11.212
You didn't do anything wrong.
I was the one who came on to you.

18:11.296 --> 18:13.589
Thank you!

18:14.215 --> 18:15.216
TOTORI'S HOTEL

18:15.300 --> 18:19.345
Even if you ask me what I am,
I'm just your average orphan.

18:19.971 --> 18:24.100
I can only remember being raised
by those vigilantes.

18:24.684 --> 18:28.021
So you were born after the Great Disaster,
and raised as an orphan?

18:28.521 --> 18:30.857
But your parents could be alive somewhere.

18:31.691 --> 18:34.277
It's not like I want to look for them.
Or meet them.

18:35.153 --> 18:38.114
I've realized something.

18:38.197 --> 18:40.450
Anything that feels good makes money.

18:41.326 --> 18:44.412
I'll earn money by getting
more clean rooms and futons.

18:44.495 --> 18:47.665
I'll have sex with the customers I like,

18:48.249 --> 18:50.168
and become the King of Hotels!

18:53.504 --> 18:57.258
[Maru]
I don't get why I can enter a human.

18:57.842 --> 19:00.636
But good thing I cleared up
that misunderstanding.

19:01.220 --> 19:05.099
I thought the only way
I was gonna get you to believe me,

19:05.183 --> 19:07.268
was by killing her with the Maru-Touch.

19:07.852 --> 19:10.396
Oh, yeah?
Wasn't it the Whatchamacallit Dive?

19:10.480 --> 19:12.607
Forget that ever happened!

19:12.690 --> 19:16.778
I knew it was bad the second I said it.

19:16.861 --> 19:19.280
[Kiruko] I remember now. Fatal Dive.

19:19.364 --> 19:21.032
[Maru] I told you to forget it!

19:22.241 --> 19:24.077
HOTEL

19:24.160 --> 19:25.203
[broom sweeping]

19:25.787 --> 19:27.080
[Kiruko] Well, see ya.

19:27.163 --> 19:28.873
The futon was really comfortable.

19:30.291 --> 19:32.377
What's up? You don't look too good.

19:32.460 --> 19:34.462
What happened to all that energy
from last night?

19:35.630 --> 19:37.799
They said the Boss didn't make it.

19:39.258 --> 19:41.260
He died early in the morning.

19:41.761 --> 19:43.763
Even though you saved him.

19:45.223 --> 19:48.768
He was so tough.
I didn't think he would die.

19:50.186 --> 19:52.855
He was a good boss. So kind to us.

19:54.357 --> 19:57.360
Well, dying is a part of life.

20:01.572 --> 20:02.824
[Kiruko] Want to join us?

20:08.204 --> 20:09.205
Okay.

20:14.377 --> 20:16.796
Then be the King of Hotels.

20:23.719 --> 20:27.557
Even a guy like that
was important to somebody.

20:29.267 --> 20:32.937
If I was born and raised in this area,

20:33.980 --> 20:35.940
I might've been one of his guys.

22:39.522 --> 22:41.232
You look better today.

22:42.024 --> 22:45.111
I was worried about something,
but it's all better now.

22:46.404 --> 22:47.405
That's good.

22:57.290 --> 22:59.333
DETECTING DETAILED POINTS

22:59.417 --> 23:01.586
COMPARISON IN PROGRESS
INSPECTION COMPLETE

23:01.669 --> 23:03.212
FEATURES - 92% MATCH
OBJECTS APPEAR IDENTICAL

23:03.796 --> 23:05.673
I found it. This is it.

23:07.425 --> 23:09.510
The footprint in this room is…

23:10.469 --> 23:11.512
Tokio's.

23:12.597 --> 23:15.016
But how? Without anyone noticing?

23:17.560 --> 23:20.813
[Tokio] I saw Asura's ghost today.

23:21.939 --> 23:23.107
Ghost?

23:23.190 --> 23:25.318
But it might have been a dream.

23:26.277 --> 23:28.738
You liked Asura, right?

23:29.405 --> 23:30.406
Yeah.

23:32.491 --> 23:36.954
But it's different to my love for you.

23:37.997 --> 23:39.081
You know that, right?

23:41.751 --> 23:42.752
Yeah.

23:42.835 --> 23:43.836
Translated by Annie Chen
